Foundation Item 
8-406 Core Item Violation 



Frequency 8-401.10 Establishing Inspection Interval. 

(A) Except as specified in ¶¶ (B) and (C) of this section, the 
REGULATORY AUTHORITY shall inspect a FOOD ESTABLISHMENT at 
least once every 6 months and twice in a season for seasonal 
operations. 

(B) The REGULATORY AUTHORITY may increase the interval 
between inspections beyond 6 months if: 

(1) The FOOD ESTABLISHMENT is fully operating under an 
APPROVED and validated HACCP PLAN as specified under 
§ 8-201.14 and ¶¶ 8-103.12(A) and (B); 

(2) The FOOD ESTABLISHMENT is assigned a less frequent 
inspection frequency based on a written RISK-based 
inspection schedule that is being uniformly applied 
throughout the jurisdiction or

